GeoNames sample and derived place indexes

Contains geographical data from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/),
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The GeoNames Gazetteer extract files are published at:
https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/
Their format and license statement are in:
https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/readme.txt

data/geonames-sample.tsv, data/admin1-sample.tsv and
data/country-info-sample.tsv contain selected complete upstream rows.
Rows were selected and sorted; their field values and row bytes were not
edited. data/sample-receipt.json records each input URL, retrieval time,
SHA-256 digest, archive member, selected identifier and output digest.
Generated indexes transform these rows into this project's JSON format.
Redistributed indexes must retain the GeoNames attribution, source link,
license link and description of the transformation.

GeoNames provides its data "as is" without warranty or any representation
of accuracy, timeliness or completeness. GeoNames does not endorse this
project. Modern place coordinates and timezone labels are not evidence of
historical jurisdiction boundaries or historical civil-clock offsets.

The sample selector and index builder are MIT, under ../LICENSE.

Historical civil-time resolution

Atlas-derived answers contain data from the Zodiacs.org historical time
atlas, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
https://github.com/zodiacs-org/engine/tree/main/atlas
The result identifies the atlas version and release date,
its GeoNames coordinate source, rule versions and primary-source citations.
The adapter copies those result fields without changing their values.
Retain that provenance with redistributed atlas-derived answers.
The atlas resolver tools and this adapter are MIT.

Other offsets use the engine's IANA tzdb histories and host Intl/ICU.
See ../LICENSING.md, GeoNames and timezone data, and ../docs/time.md.
